      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregularity in the hydraulic circuit pressure spikes on your F-150 could be due to component wear such as seals or bearings, contaminated transmission fluid, or a damaged pump impeller or valve. Another possible cause might be issues with the transmission control module or connector problems that are affecting the software-driven aspects of the hydraulic circuit. It’s also advisable to check if the scan tool is properly calibrated and experienced inconsistencies. A professional diagnostic would help pinpoint the exact issue.",
