      "content": "If the solenoids and valves are in good shape, intermittent issues could be due to electrical gremlins such as wiring shorts or poor connections, particularly those affecting the transmit fault detection circuit. These could lead to stalling under specific conditions and subsequently cause the spikes. Another possibility might be the fluctuating engine load impacting the shift control unit's response when tied to engine duty cycles. An intermittent fuel pressure issue could also mimic these symptoms. Close attention to scan tool data logging under different loads and conditions can reveal whether these are sporadic electrical issues or related to specific operational circumstances. It’s always wise to have a professional IMA (Integrated Motor Assembly) specialist to examine these intricate possibilities.",
